c Graph H_5 of Theorem 1 in 'The CLIQUES Algorithm Is Not Output-Polynomial' (Sec. 3)
c target n = 100; nearest H_k has n = 2k^2+9k = 95 vertices (k = 5)
c maximal cliques: 481 (Lemma bound (k+1)(2k(k+3)+1) = 486 <= n^2 = 9025)
c every run of CLIQUES makes at least 2^(k+1)-1 = 63 recursive calls (one run with min-label tie-breaking and increasing order: 2161)
c vertices: guards g_i = 1..5; core a_i = k+2i-1, b_i = k+2i (6..15); witnesses 16..95, 8 per core vertex in the order a_1, b_1, a_2, ...
p edge 95 1205
